 "researcher_notes": "MVP Boost adds compression to the existing Mountain Valley mainline. It has no row of its own. The mainline row P0220 and the Southgate, Greene and Interconnect rows are different projects. A Mountain Valley Pipeline press release from October 23, 2025 says the company asked the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission to approve the project. It adds compression at three existing compressor stations in West Virginia and builds a new compressor station next to the mainline in Montgomery County, Virginia. The release does not name the West Virginia stations or the new station, so the locations stay general. It gives 600 thousand dekatherms per day of added capacity, construction from the winter of 2026 to 2027, and service in mid-2028. Mountain Valley Pipeline LLC will build and own it. An EQT investor presentation from October 2025 says utilities drove the demand, backed by power generation and data center demand in Northern Virginia. That is a general mention, so the data center tag is medium. Compression only, so length is 0 with no diameter and no route. No cost was found."
